EmailTemplate.textOnly:
Hello {!Contact.FirstName},

If you have decided to delay your first semester at Arizona State University, you should defer your admission. Consider your options carefully before taking this step.
Typical reasons for deferring your admission include: involuntary military activation, ecclesiastical service or volunteer service.

The admission deferment guarantees only admission into the university and not necessarily admission to a particular major or program of study. You may defer your admission for a period of up to five terms or two and a half years.

To learn more or to defer your admission, visit students.asu.edu/deferadmissions.

Sincerely,

{!User.Recruiter_Full_Name__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Title__c}
Admission Services
{!User.Recruiter_Email__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Phone__c}

If you have any additional information or questions related to this, please reply to this email.

